! REPRODUCER: strap_asm.py assembles a DD in a DECIMAL mode as a binary
! integer.  Found 2026-11-15 transcribing C22-6578 Problem 2.8
! (problem_2_8.strap), whose D and E subfields are (DU, 24, 8) and
! (DU, 48, 8).  docs/NEXT.md has the section.
!
! THE RULE, C22-6531 printed pp.28-29 (PDF 29-30), "Decimal Signed VFL":
!   "The two decimal modes in DD and DDI statements represent the only
!   cases in which Strap-1 converts numbers to an internal decimal
!   radix."  Example a: "DD(D), -9534812 ... A 4-bit sign byte is
!   formed.  Decimal-to-decimal conversion."  Example c: "DD(D, , 8),
!   432E3 ... Four binary zeros are inserted in the zone positions of
!   each byte."  Decimal Unsigned: "The numerical conversion is just as
!   in decimal signed mode except for the omission of the sign byte."
!
! WHAT EACH WORD SHOULD BE, by that rule, and what strap_asm makes:
!
!   DU8    DD(DU,16,8), 12       0102   digits 1, 2       strap_asm 000C
!   DU4    DD(DU,16,4), 1234     1234                     strap_asm 04D2
!   DUE    DD(DU,48,8), 000125   000000010205             strap_asm 00000000007D
!   DS4    DD(D,16,4), -123      1238   digits and S=1    strap_asm FF85
!   BUCTL  DD(BU,16,8), 12       000C   the binary control, right
!
! DS4's sign byte is S T U V with S the sign (Reference Manual printed
! p.36) and 1 for minus; FF85 is a two's complement, which is not a
! 7030 number form at all.
!
! THE HOST STRAP II (strap/strap2, "ASM=strap2") ASSEMBLES ALL FIVE AS
! THE RULE SAYS -- OBSERVED 0102, 1234, 0000 0001 0205, 1238, 000C.
!
! FIXED IN strap_asm 2026-11-23 (the "strap_asm ..." column above is the
! before).  The STRAP II rule is C28-6129 printed p.15 (PDF 19), which
! prints "DD(DU, 12, 4),12 / 000000010010", and printed pp.29-30.  The
! registered run is two runs of this one deck, strap_asm and ASM=strap2,
! with the same five values; tests/check_dd_decimal_mode.py has the
! rows and the injections.  The program is one BEW, $.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   BEW, $
        SLC, 1010.0
DU8     DD(DU,16,8), 12
        SLC, 1011.0
DU4     DD(DU,16,4), 1234
        SLC, 1012.0
DUE     DD(DU,48,8), 000125
        SLC, 1013.0
DS4     DD(D,16,4), -123
        SLC, 1014.0
BUCTL   DD(BU,16,8), 12
        END, START
